WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.190
Welcome to Peer Reviews. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Find defects early using structured reviews of work products.

2
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:19.540
Consider this scenario. An architecture design is approved without technical scrutiny. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:29.670
Start with two steps: Choose critical work products. Then Prepare criteria and reviewers. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:39.970
Continue with Record findings and suggested fixes. Then Verify resolution and trends. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:59.740
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous review checklist, defect log, closure evidence tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: mistaking casual agreement for a documented peer review; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:13.990
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
